    LLM: 'Game: Twenty-Six. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Twenty-Six is a trick-taking round game in the Cucumber/Twenty-Two family. Suits irrelevant; rank A-K-Q-J-10-9-8-7-6-5-4-3-2. Players lead single cards or sets of equal rank; others must equal or beat the highest played, or play lowest. Winner of the last trick is penalised (e.g. keeps losing card or gets penalty points). For 2-6 players, 52 cards.',
    objective: 'Avoid winning the last trick (or avoid collecting penalty cards).',
    gameplay: 'Play clockwise. Lead single cards or sets of equal rank. Others must play cards equal or higher to the highest played if possible; else play lowest. Highest play wins the trick. Last trick is penalised.',
